### ===========================================================
### LiteLLM – Cache Tests
### Run "Cache warm-up" first, then "Cache hit check".
### Check litellm logs: docker compose logs litellm --tail 50
### ===========================================================

@baseUrl = http://localhost:4000
@apiKey = {{LITELLM_MASTER_KEY}}
@model = gpt-5.4-mini


# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# CACHE STATUS
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

### Cache ping – confirms Redis is reachable from LiteLLM
GET {{baseUrl}}/cache/ping
Authorization: Bearer {{apiKey}}


# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# EXACT CACHE TEST
# Step 1: run warm-up, Step 2: run hit check
# Expect: hit check returns same content faster, logged as cache hit
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

### Step 1 – Cache warm-up (sends request to provider)
POST {{baseUrl}}/v1/chat/completions
Authorization: Bearer {{apiKey}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "model": "{{model}}",
  "messages": [
    { "role": "user", "content": "Reply with exactly this text and nothing else: cache-test-12345" }
  ]
}

###

### Step 2 – Cache hit check (identical request – should serve from Redis)
POST {{baseUrl}}/v1/chat/completions
Authorization: Bearer {{apiKey}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "model": "{{model}}",
  "messages": [
    { "role": "user", "content": "Reply with exactly this text and nothing else: cache-test-12345" }
  ]
}


# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# CACHE MISS CONTROLS
# These should NOT hit cache – confirms cache key boundaries
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

### Miss – different prompt content
POST {{baseUrl}}/v1/chat/completions
Authorization: Bearer {{apiKey}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "model": "{{model}}",
  "messages": [
    { "role": "user", "content": "Reply with exactly this text and nothing else: cache-test-99999" }
  ]
}

###

### Miss – different model (same prompt as warm-up)
POST {{baseUrl}}/v1/chat/completions
Authorization: Bearer {{apiKey}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "model": "gpt-5.4-mini",
  "messages": [
    { "role": "user", "content": "Reply with exactly this text and nothing else: cache-test-12345" }
  ]
}

###

### Miss – added temperature param (changes cache key)
POST {{baseUrl}}/v1/chat/completions
Authorization: Bearer {{apiKey}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "model": "{{model}}",
  "temperature": 0.5,
  "messages": [
    { "role": "user", "content": "Reply with exactly this text and nothing else: cache-test-12345" }
  ]
}
